Here's a quote from the rgrn FAQ:

>4.4Q:   My game crashed and I lost my character! Is there anything
        I can do?

>4.4A:

>Maybe. There is a program that comes with NetHack called "recover"
>that may be able to restore a crashed game, depending on how NetHack
>was compiled. Check for a file called "recover.txt" for an explanation.
>On some platforms, "recover" may have been incorporated into the game
>itself, and restarting the game using the same character name will
>work (if the crash was recoverable from to start with).

From the number of times that the words "maybe" and "may" are
used here, it would seem that the (presumably knowledgeable)
people who compiled the FAQ don't think that Recover will necessarily
work every time. And my personal experience confirms this. So,
especially if your system/build is prone to crash, I think it makes
sense to keep a backup of the save file as an extra layer of safety.

Whether it'd be too tempting to use the backup in case of YASD
is something that each person will have to decide by looking
deep within themselves; also whether they're willing to risk the
opprobrium of someone on a newsgroup who thinks that anyone
who backs up a save file must be doing it to cheat. But I
don't think anyone should be absolutely confident in Recover
until they've verified that it works on their platform.


